From 847ae449df6d60d2a48d471a79e14de9961713f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:53:01 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Menu: previews that follow the pad in hand, Resolution, Sharp
 text, a game's pictures

- The previews and the button hints read the controller in the player's
  hands (Layer::menu_gamepad(): the one last pressed or pushed, any
  connected), not only player 1's: the menu answers every pad, so a pad
  chosen for player 2 drove the menu while its previews said to connect
  one. When the game does not read that pad, the preview says so.
- Resolution: close-ups of one place of the paused frame at x1, x2, the step
  below and as paused. The lower steps are worked out with a tent filter
  (within about 1 % of the game drawn at x1, measured on Dissidia's text and
  pictures). The place is where a lower resolution changes the picture most,
  nearer the middle counting more, the 2D interface left out: the renderer
  notes where the last whole frame drew it (interface_rects()).
- Sharp text: a block of the game's own text, its PSP-sized letters enlarged
  (Off) and its glyphs drawn again at the resolution's scale (On), from the
  glyphs Sharp text keeps (fonts::text_sample).
- GameProfile::setting_pictures: two pictures of the game, off and on, for
  a setting of the port's that the paused game cannot show both ways.
- GameProfile::pause_credit: lines at the pause screen's bottom right.
- The page's card (Network status, About, ...) stays at the side panel's
  bottom from row to row; text fields name themselves in the panel; the
  descriptions that said <prefix>_ give the variable's name.
- <prefix>_TRACE_MENU: where the Resolution close-ups went, and why.

Built and run with Dissidia 012 (Windows, clang) at 1920x1088 and 1440x816,
with the input script's virtual gamepads. Not run: a real pad, Linux,
Android, the framework's own build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
